load ../credential-unwrap-confinement.maude

--- Fixture shape. One credential h1 wraps TWO types under the same key --
--- tPatient and tBilling -- which is the ordinary case and the reason type
--- narrowing has anything to say.
---
---   reviewer   secret-cleared, NOT durable   (a model provider)
---   mailout    public-only,    NOT durable
---   factbase   secret-cleared, DURABLE       <-- the adversarial setting
---
--- The fact base is deliberately cleared for `secret`, so no theorem below is
--- carried by clearance. A single-tenant on-prem deployment plausibly clears
--- it, and that is exactly the deployment where today's design would let
--- plaintext back into facts.value_json with every IFC check satisfied.

--- Coverage: the region opens when the grant names the envelope's type, and a
--- cleared non-durable sink inside it receives the plaintext. The mechanism
--- works -- an `ask Reviewer to summarize rec` inside the region is fine.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(reviewer, secret) sinkLabel(mailout, public) sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, reviewer)
  =>* C:Cfg delivered(v1, reviewer, secret) .

--- Coverage: LEGAL EXIT 1. A granted declassify carries a bounded projection
--- out of the region, and that result reaches the durable fact base. Together
--- with the next search this is what keeps T2/T3 from being vacuous -- the
--- region is not a dead end.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  grantDeclassify(tPatient) sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) declassifyReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, factbase)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedPlain(v1, public) .

--- Coverage: LEGAL EXIT 2. A value derived inside the region is re-sealed and
--- persisted as ciphertext. This is the route the syntax spells
--- `seal rec.severity ... -> sev` before `record`.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) deriveReq(v1, v2) resealReq(v2, tPatient, h1)
  sinkReq(v2, factbase)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedCipher(v2) .

--- Coverage: a grant for tPatient presented against a tBilling envelope
--- REFUSES rather than opening. T1's positive face.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tBilling, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  openReq(v1, tBilling)
  =>* C:Cfg refused(v1) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture. Under the possession-based grant of SS14, ONE
--- grant on h1 opens a tBilling envelope although nothing about billing was
--- ever granted. T1's bite: the same credential wraps many types and a bare
--- `unwrap` reaches all of them.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT-POSSESSION :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tBilling, h1) grantUnwrapAny(h1)
  openReq(v1, tPatient)
  =>* C:Cfg holds(v1, secret) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture. Plaintext at its sealed label lands in the
--- durable fact base, because the fact base is cleared for it and nothing
--- else objects. The label was carried faithfully the whole way -- carriage
--- is not violated here, which is precisely why T2/T3 do not follow from it.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT-POSSESSION :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrapAny(h1)
  sinkLabel(factbase, secret) openReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, factbase)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedPlain(v1, secret) .

--- THEOREM T1. A grant issued for tPatient never opens a tBilling envelope
--- under the same credential, however the search interleaves. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tBilling, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(reviewer, secret) sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tBilling) sinkReq(v1, reviewer)
  =>* inRegion(v1, secret, tBilling) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM T2. A durable sink is closed to in-region plaintext ALTHOUGH IT IS
--- CLEARED FOR THE LABEL. This is the refusal the proposal adds over SS13, and
--- the one an earlier cut of this model missed: the generic sink route reached
--- the fact base while a separate `record` route was the only thing checked.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, factbase)
  =>* delivered(v1, factbase, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM T3. Plaintext is never persisted at its sealed label, with BOTH
--- exits available and a direct durable-sink request present. Every route to
--- a durable sink funnels through persistedPlain, so this covers them all.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  grantDeclassify(tPatient) sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) declassifyReq(v1, tPatient) resealReq(v1, tPatient, h1)
  sinkReq(v1, factbase)
  =>* persistedPlain(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM T3, on a DERIVED value. A field computed from the record inherits
--- the confinement, so re-sealing is the only way to persist it. Without this
--- the theorem would cover only the value that entered the region.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  grantDeclassify(tPatient) sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) deriveReq(v1, v2) sinkReq(v2, factbase)
  =>* persistedPlain(v2, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: IFC still applies INSIDE the region. Secret plaintext never reaches
--- the public-only sink; confinement is additional to the sticky boundary,
--- not a substitute for it. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(mailout, public)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, mailout)
  =>* delivered(v1, mailout, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: CUSTODY IS REQUIRED, as for every operation in the vocabulary. With
--- the grant present but no custodian, nothing opens. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  openReq(v1, tPatient)
  =>* inRegion(v1, secret, tPatient) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: the escape is GRANTED, not structural. With no declassify grant, no
--- in-region value ever becomes ordinary held data -- so exit 1 is a governed
--- hole rather than a property of the region. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-UNWRAP-CONFINEMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  sinkLabel(factbase, secret)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) declassifyReq(v1, tPatient) sinkReq(v1, factbase)
  =>* holds(v1, public) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
